{
	"_comment": "Inline scalar ownership vectors of the TOML batch writer, replayed by _shared/lua/test/toml_inline_scalar_vectors_contract.lua on macOS and Linux. Each vector gives the file bytes (source), the batch rows and what two entry points answer: the source hint step source_inline_scalar_parents(source, rows), which names the inline tables a direct scalar write may address (expect.hint_parents is that set; [] means none), and the writer's prepare step prepare_batch(path, rows, {read source}). expect.ok is acceptance of prepare; when false no bytes come back (a raised refusal counts). content is the exact candidate; decoded lists paths of the decoded candidate whose value must equal value (negative_zero also checks the IEEE sign); idempotent means preparing the same rows on the candidate answers the candidate again. A value {\"$number\": \"text\"} is the number the text spells, with inf, -inf and nan for the non-finite ones JSON cannot carry. Converted from toml_batch_existing_key_contract.lua.",
	"entry_point": "source_inline_scalar_parents(source, rows) -> set of inline parent tables, then the writer's prepare step on (source, rows)",
	"drivers": {
		"macos": "Replays every vector.",
		"linux": "Replays every vector.",
		"windows": "Not ported: one AHK consumer must call the Windows writer's inline hint step and prepare step on (source, rows) and decode the candidate for the decoded checks."
	},
